25. The following punishments may be inflicted by a court:
(a) death;
(b) imprisonment;
(c) corporal punishment;
(d) fine;
(e) forfeiture;
(f) payment of compensation;
(g) finding security to keep the peace and be of good behavior or to come up for judgment;
(h) any other punishment provided by this Code or by any other law.
